# Justified exceptions for Trivy (CI-2, docs/plan/11-ci-security.md).
# One finding ID per line, each preceded by a comment explaining why it is accepted.
# Every entry must also be listed in docs/security/README.md and in the report.

# krb5-libs 1.21.1-10.el9_8.1 in the six service images (base ubi9/openjdk-21-runtime:1.24).
# The fix (1.21.1-10.el9_9.2) is only in the subscription RHEL repositories, not yet in the public
# UBI repositories, so `microdnf update` in the Dockerfiles cannot install it (checked 13/11/2026).
# The package cannot be removed: libcurl, cyrus-sasl and cups-libs link it.
# All the CVEs below are in the KDC or kadmind (Kerberos server daemons, not installed in the
# images) or in Kerberos authentication, which no service uses.
# The entries expire on 30/11/2026: the CI fails again then, to check whether UBI ships the fix.
CVE-2026-107364 exp:2026-11-30
